{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9832","id":4763426071,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABG-wdFw","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9832","diff_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9832.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9832.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9832","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9832/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9832/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9832/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/statuses/4e533e768d5342e705976bd704cfe63af6b99eed","number":9832,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[grug] Leave ragged MoE transport rows unwritten when nothing reads them","user":{"login":"mcwitt","id":319411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTQxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt","html_url":"https://github.com/mcwitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The ragged all-to-all MoE stops filling and overwriting transport rows that no consumer reads, and on GPU builds its dispatch buffer with one scatter.\n\nThe expert chunks write disjoint rows of the dispatch and return buffers, but the custom VJP around `ragged_all_to_all` differentiated each write as an overwrite, so every layer's backward spent a [TK, H] select, a [TK, H] add and a [TK, H] zero fill on rows the next chunk would ignore. Each written row holds nothing before its one write, and for such a row an overwrite has the derivative of an add, so the transpose now passes the output cotangent through unchanged. With every consumer reading only rows a collective wrote, the buffers need no fill. On GPU they come from a Triton kernel that writes nothing; elsewhere they are zero-filled. Each buffer is tied to a loop-carried value, because a buffer with no inputs is loop invariant: XLA would hoist it out of the layer loop and then copy it into every layer's output slot. Dropped and padded slots get combine weight 0, and the combine and dispatch-gradient sums skip them.\n\nOn GPU, a Triton kernel builds the expert-sorted dispatch buffer by reading each token's row once and writing it to the token's accepted slots; the gather it replaces read every row topk times. The kernel's weighted form is unused until #9833 builds the backward's output cotangents with it. The gather-sum's forward kernel now loops over 1024-wide hidden tiles, which keeps more programs resident, and each element still sums its K rows in order.\n\nA GPU test runs the ragged layer with forced drops and padding, once with every transport buffer zero-filled and once NaN-filled. Outputs, drop counts and all gradients, including a recompute, must be finite and bitwise equal.\n\nOutputs, drops and every gradient are bitwise unchanged across drops, padding, one-hot routing and hero per-shard shapes on GB200x4. One MoE layer's forward and backward is 4.4-4.8% faster, and the compiler temp drops by 1.37 GB per layer. At the hero's per-GPU routed shape on GB200 (TK = 524288 assignments of width H = 3072, the routed experts' latent width), the scatter takes 0.535 ms (6.6 TB/s), and the gather-sum forward 0.508 ms against 0.574 ms before.\n\nIn #9708's series (one 64-GPU hero rack, restore step-180000, seed 0, 100 steps), the unfilled buffers shortened the step from 13.737 to 13.542 s (+1.44%) on a base with #9831's remat flag. The dispatch scatter, measured together with its use in #9833's backward on a base that also had #9833, #9834 and earlier versions of #9829's and #9830's kernels, shortened the step from 12.875 to 12.730 s (+1.14%).\n\nSplit from #9708. Part of #9636.\n","labels":[{"id":10166074947,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACXfH-Qw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agent-generated","name":"agent-generated","description":"Created by automation/agent","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11981276996,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACyiPHRA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agentic-lint","name":"agentic-lint","description":"Local agentic lint review completed","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-06T19:07:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T19:11:21Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"00063372742fcca5eef3e69b496fa26b3b8ad0dd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dlwh","id":9633,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9633?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh","html_url":"https://github.com/dlwh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlw